{"parentUuid":"6a8dcfad-342a-49c3-89c5-a86ea04a7d83","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgT7Ug6cvyyf6P1rk1TuY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Everything is committed in 7 signed commits across 2 branches. `make ai-checks` passed before each commit, and nothing is pushed.\n\n## Commits\n**`chore/speckit-setup`**\n- `e4bcc9e` build: install GitHub spec-kit 1.2.3 with the Claude integration\n- `57c2b57` docs: ratify the Gravespeaker spec-kit constitution\n- `e346e3a` docs: limit agent output to what the user must act on\n- `a1e8487` docs: add social media search for recent deaths to the v2 PRD (cutoff set to 2010)\n\n**`test/benchmark-fixtures`** (branched from `main`, independent of the spec-kit branch)\n- `ec79bd1` chore: exclude benchmark fixtures from Semgrep scans\n- `ab0c068` test: add 24 headstone fixtures with ground truth for the benchmark\n- `36179f0` docs: set fixture rules for notable people and modern graves\n\n## Fixture set: 17 modern, 7 historic\n- **Modern graves (17):** 11 clean, 4 weathered, 2 edge cases.\n  - `chambers-2011` died after the 2010 cutoff, so it's ready for the v2 social search.\n  - `currens-living` is a stone made before death: both spouses have only birth dates and may still be alive. The app must not research or narrate them.\n  - New name traps: `hansen-1978` is close to an MLB pitcher who died a year earlier, and the two Newman stones share a surname and cemetery.\n- **Historic stones (7):**\n  - Two legible: the Cunningham colonial pair.\n  - Partly legible: `ellis-1818`, `jenks-1882`, `bybee-pioneer`.\n  - Two fully illegible 19th-century stones for the \"can't read it\" case.\n- **Removed:** `archbald-tomb`, plus Leavitt, Coney, Blanchard, Skinner, Cora and Bowen, to cut the old-stone share.\n- **New `era` field** in `manifest.json` lets the benchmark report modern and historic scores separately.\n\n## Needs your eyes\n- **Dates on the illegible stones:** Commons doesn't give them. I picked both because they look 19th-century, but \"early 19th\" isn't confirmed.\n- **Semgrep:** `.semgrepignore` replaces Semgrep's built-in ignore list, so it pulls in `.gitignore` to keep `node_modules` and `build` excluded. I haven't re-run the scan to confirm it now fits under the size limit.\n- **One commit-format slip:** a bullet in `ab0c068` wraps onto a second line, which the commit skill forbids. commitlint passed it. Fixing it needs a rebase, which I won't do without your go-ahead."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1122,"cache_read_input_tokens":239659,"output_tokens":974,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":42},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1122,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":974,"cache_read_input_tokens":239659,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1122,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1122},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgT7UfPxtmXJpPy6aqLgm","requestRef":"238c757f-65e3-40ac-af86-71af2f4a2d6f","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","attributionSkill":"generate-commit-message","type":"assistant","uuid":"28f33e10-0bec-4b63-9e57-835246f0e765","timestamp":"2026-10-27T17:10:25.570Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"e8fe1454-894d-486c-ada2-536b95330a4e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/anchildress1/git_personal/gravespeaker","sessionId":"a78fbb29-c412-483a-b679-0722adb27f13","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"test/benchmark-fixtures"}
