{"parentUuid":"ecf80cbf-266d-4af4-a376-636a6b52ec3a","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgT7wcXKycQ1vwZGSzcQy","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The `.semgrepignore` I added doesn't fix this. Guardian ignores that file entirely.\n\n- **How Guardian works:** it scans whatever files my tool calls touch. Its state log shows it trying to send the fixture photos (`brockelbank-1996.jpg`, `coney-17xx.jpg`) that my shell commands copied and deleted, and they're over its size limit.\n- **What was actually skipped:** only photos, which can't hold code findings. The text files in this turn (`.prettierignore`, `.semgrepignore`) were scanned.\n- **Not scanned at all:** the review page's `index.html`, because it sits outside the repo.\n- **The file is dead config:** nothing else in the repo runs Semgrep — no CI job, no Lefthook hook, no Makefile target. So `.semgrepignore` does nothing.\n- **What to expect:** the warning will come back whenever I touch fixture photos. It goes quiet once the image work is done.\n\n**Proposed fix:** drop commit `ec79bd1` (the `.semgrepignore` commit) as part of the fixture squash I asked about last turn. That's one history rewrite on an unpushed branch, and it removes the dead file along with the 24-photo set. Say \"squash\" and I'll do both."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":426,"cache_read_input_tokens":309830,"output_tokens":602,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":180},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":426,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":602,"cache_read_input_tokens":309830,"cache_creation_input_tokens":426,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":426},"t