{"parentUuid":"989c8306-8f67-49af-a0d2-83a9f4f9c027","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgT8DKAyjDiA5sshjspWo","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`manifest.json` now has a `text` field holding the full carved inscription, which replaces `notes`. Branch history is rewritten, and dead config is gone. Everything is committed and `make ai-checks` passes.\n\n## `fixtures/manifest.json`\n- **`text`:** one line per carved line, with `[?]` for a word that can't be read. `illegible-marble` has `text: null`.\n- **Unchanged:** `people` (name, born, died), as you asked.\n- **Kept your edits:** the `reviewed: true` you set on `chambers-2011` and `gonzalez-2021`.\n- **Lost:** the trap descriptions that lived in `notes` (the Jr/III name pair, the living spouse, \"46 YEARS\" being the marriage length). Say if you want them back as a separate field.\n- **Check closely:** the Ellis age (\"ag'd 11\") and the Cunningham \"60th\" were the hardest reads.\n\n## Review page\n- Each card now has an editable **Full text on stone** box.\n- Stones you marked `reviewed: true` in the file count as done.\n- Same link: https://claude.ai/artifact/2xtJSGENbbvQBMcHxyGKsZ\n\n## `test/benchmark-fixtures` history (unpushed)\n- `c1cc170` test: add 9 headstone fixtures with ground truth for the benchmark\n- `2810dd1` docs: set fixture rules for the headstone benchmark\n- `0a2fb9b` build: keep benchmark fixtures out of the Docker build context\n- `138e1a1` chore: drop gitignore entries for hosts and files this repo never uses\n\nThe 24-photo intermediate set and the `.semgrepignore` commit are gone. I checked the final files against a backup taken before the rewrite, and they match.\n\n## Dead config removed\n- **`.semgrepignore`:** nothing in the repo runs Semgrep, and Guardian ignores the file.\n- **`.gitignore`:**\n  - Dropped the `.output`, `.vercel`, `.netlify` and `.wrangler` entries; this app only deploys to Cloud Run.\n  - Dropped `!.env.test`; that file doesn't exist.\n- **Also added:** `fixtures` to `.dockerignore`. The Docker build was uploading the 14 MB of photos every time, though they never reached the final image."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":672,"cache_read_input_tokens":322585,"output_tokens":783,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":672,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":783,"cache_read_input_tokens":322585,"cache_creation_input_tokens":672,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":672},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgT8DJWJ9tNQ3ArxLgmMy","requestRef":"8d0603f7-5257-4e29-aa78-bd5f269467d4","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"960236d8-7e10-4d59-85c8-39b2a7c6ef3c","timestamp":"2026-10-27T17:20:01.992Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"e8fe1454-894d-486c-ada2-536b95330a4e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/anchildress1/git_personal/gravespeaker","sessionId":"a78fbb29-c412-483a-b679-0722adb27f13","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"test/benchmark-fixtures"}
