{"parentUuid":"04da67c0-459d-4215-b308-6d0ee9f00df2","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgTBVKxQWwJZivsepdm66","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2041,"cache_read_input_tokens":349692,"output_tokens":1452,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":243},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2041,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1452,"cache_read_input_tokens":349692,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2041,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2041},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":10414,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgTBVKPft3MxfXSLsvVjA","requestRef":"31c53b88-ba19-42e3-8662-477743f45233","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"e5ec2bd0-61be-4114-9388-74f45720aaf4","timestamp":"2026-10-27T18:03:03.410Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"e8fe1454-894d-486c-ada2-536b95330a4e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/anchildress1/git_personal/gravespeaker/fixtures","sessionId":"a78fbb29-c412-483a-b679-0722adb27f13","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"test/benchmark-fixtures"}
{"parentUuid":"e5ec2bd0-61be-4114-9388-74f45720aaf4","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgTBVKxQWwJZivsepdm66","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Gemma 4 reads clean modern headstones as well as Gemini. Its one real failure is the two-person stone. These numbers come from a throwaway script in my scratch folder; the real `scripts/benchmark.ts` isn't built yet.\n\n## Results (9 fixtures, same prompt for every model, one run each)\n\n| Fixture | gemma-4-26b | gemma-4-31b | gemini-3.8-flash |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| chambers-2011 | 3/3 | 3/3 | 3/3 |\n| gonzalez-2021 | 3/3 | 3/3 | 3/3 |\n| guo-2025 | 3/3 | 3/3 | 3/3 |\n| hildebrand-iii-2018 | 3/3 | 3/3 | 3/3 |\n| hildebrand-jr-2015 | 3/3 | 3/3 | 0/3 |\n| **holmquist-2024** | **0/6** | **0/6** | **6/6** |\n| cunningham-1752 | 3/3 | timed out | 3/3 |\n| ellis-1818 | 2/3 | 2/3 | 2/3 |\n| illegible-marble | 1/1 | 1/1 | 1/1 |\n| **Name and date fields correct** | **75%** | **72%** | **86%** |\n| Average time per photo | 34.7 s | 55.0 s | 14.5 s |\n\nA score like 3/3 counts name, birth date and death date for each person. `illegible-marble` scores 1/1 when the model correctly reports no legible person.\n\n## What the misses actually are\n- **Holmquist (two people on one stone):** both Gemma models read every date correctly. They left the shared surname \"HOLMQUIST\" (carved once at the top) off both names. Gemini attached it to both names correctly.\n- **Ellis:** all three models read 1818 as **1848**. I zoomed in on the stone and it clearly says 1818, so the answer key stands. This is a real misread by every model.\n- **Hildebrand Jr, Gemini:** it wrote \"LE ROY\" for \"LEROY\". Its dates were right, but my scoring zeroes a person whose name doesn't match.\n- **Timeout:** `gemma-4-31b-it` spent more than 4 minutes on the colonial Cunningham slate and was cut off.\n- **Full-text accuracy is about 94% for all three models.** Holmquist pulls it down: the models read the two columns in a different order than my answer key.\n\n## Scoring decisions you should know about\n- Names are matched ignoring capitalisation and punctuation. Models write names in capitals as carved; the answer key uses normal capitalisation.\n- \"Mr\" is ignored, so \"M.r ANDREW CUNNINGHAM\" counts as a match.\n- Chinese characters in a name are ignored, so \"郭俊士 Jiunn-Shih Guo\" matches \"Jiunn-Shih Guo\".\n- These are my choices. They should become explicit rules in the real benchmark.\n\n## What this means\n- **Two-person stones:** this is the requirement to adjust if we stay on Gemma, unless a prompt change fixes the shared surname. Gemini handles them; Gemma doesn't.\n- **Speed:** the faster Gemma model (26B) takes about 35 s per photo against Gemini's 15 s. That's slow for a live phone flow.\n\nThe raw answers are in `/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-anchildress1-git-personal-gravespeaker/a78fbb29-c412-483a-b679-0722adb27f13/scratchpad/bench/results.json`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2041,"cache_read_input_tokens":349692,"output_tokens":1452,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":243},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2041,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1452,"cache_read_input_tokens":349692,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2041,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2041},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgTBVKPft3MxfXSLsvVjA","requestRef":"31c53b88-ba19-42e3-8662-477743f45233","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"31276113-d112-4e6b-b0a7-1fe720b11b2b","timestamp"