{"parentUuid":"03147502-24df-416d-9a9d-87bddf3acdf8","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"PreToolUse:WebSearch","toolUseID":"toolu_01A97y7rBadYJzmWBCcMX41j","hookEvent":"PreToolUse","content":"","stdout":"{}\n","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"python3 \"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/hooks/pretooluse.py\"","durationMs":40},"type":"attachment","uuid":"1bae20aa-a20a-43da-99b0-a044ce525af8","timestamp":"2026-10-27T18:18:22.451Z","session_id":"e8fe1454-894d-486c-ada2-536b95330a4e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/anchildress1/git_personal/gravespeaker","sessionId":"a78fbb29-c412-483a-b679-0722adb27f13","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"test/benchmark-fixtures"}
{"parentUuid":"215e8835-f7cb-4d6b-b165-abd3903573b5","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"35537cc9-ba97-458d-9db8-2b66ba5461e6","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01A97y7rBadYJzmWBCcMX41j","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Cloud Run GPU support NVIDIA L4 general availability pricing\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"google cloud run nvidia gpu\",\"url\":\"https://www.infoq.com/news/2025/06/google-cloud-run-nvidia-gpu\"},{\"title\":\"Jump to Content\",\"url\":\"https://cloud.google.com/blog/products/serverless/cloud-run-gpus-are-now-generally-available\"},{\"title\":\"cloud run gpus are now generally available\",\"url\":\"https://cloud.google.com/blog/ja/products/serverless/cloud-run-gpus-are-now-generally-available\"},{\"title\":\"GPU support for services\",\"url\":\"https://docs.cloud.google.com/run/docs/configuring/services/gpu?hl=en\"},{\"title\":\"GPU support for services\",\"url\":\"https://docs.cloud.google.com/run/docs/configuring/services/gpu\"},{\"title\":\"GPU support for services\",\"url\":\"https://docs.cloud.google.com/run/docs/configuring/services/gpu?authuser=1\"},{\"title\":\"GPU support for services\",\"url\":\"https://docs.cloud.google.com/run/docs/configuring/services/gpu?authuser=0\"},{\"title\":\"GPU support for services\",\"url\":\"https://docs.cloud.google.com/run/docs/configuring/services/gpu-zonal-redundancy?authuser=2\"},{\"title\":\"GPU support for worker pools\",\"url\":\"https://docs.cloud.google.com/run/docs/configuring/workerpools/gpu\"},{\"title\":\"Configure GPUs for Cloud Run jobs\",\"url\":\"https://docs.cloud.google.com/run/docs/configuring/jobs/gpu\"}]\n\nThe search confirmed GA for Cloud Run GPUs on NVIDIA L4 but did not return the actual price figures.\n\n- **GA status:** Google's GA announcement says the L4 is open to all customers without a quota request, and GPU support is now covered by the Cloud Run SLA (Cloud Run GPUs are now available to everyone for NVIDIA L4 GPUs, with no quota request required). Coverage now extends to the SLA, which is a change from the earlier preview period.\n- **Enabling it:** Setup is a single flag or checkbox, simply use --gpu 1 from the Cloud Run command line, or check the \"GPU\" checkbox in the console.\n- **Pricing levers:** Zonal redundancy is on by default. Turning it off gives a lower rate in exchange for best-effort failover during a zonal outage (you can turn off zonal redundancy and benefit from a lower price for best-effort failover of your GPU workloads). Billing is per-instance and you must use instance-based billing to use the GPU feature, minimum instances are charged at the full rate even when idle.\n- **Regions:** Five regions were listed at GA: us-central1, europe-west1, europe-west4, asia-southeast1, and asia-south1. The current docs also list us-east4 and mark some regions as invitation-only or quota-dependent, so check the docs for your target region.\n- **Quota:** New projects get a small default allotment. Projects using Cloud Run nvidia-l4 GPUs in a region for the first time are automatically granted 3 GPU quota (zonal redundancy off) when the first deployment is created. Additional GPUs require a quota increase request.\n- **Newer hardware:** The current docs also list an NVIDIA RTX PRO 6000 Blackwell option, which is still in Preview.\n- **Pricing gap:** None of the results gave the per-second L4 rates. A commenter noted that third-party providers such as Runpod can have hourly rates for L4, A100, and H100 GPUs can be significantly lower than Google's, even when considering Google's per-second billing. For exact figures, use the Cloud Run pricing page, which the GPU docs point to for GPU rates. A follow-up search aimed at that page would be the next step.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"d771cf0e-82ea-48af-8687-fae9afcbd6f9","timestamp":"2026-10-27T18:18:29.889Z","toolUseResult":{"query":"Cloud Run GPU support NVIDIA L4 general availability pricing","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01NKHW3mG52BJXmUbf3f2pLS","content":[{"title":"google cloud run nvidia gpu","url":"https://www.infoq.com/news/2025/06/google-cloud-run-nvidia-gpu"},{"title":"Jump to Content","url":"https://cloud.google.com/blog/products/serverless/cloud-run-gpus-are-now-generally-available"},{"title":"cloud run gpus are now generally available","url":"https://cloud.google.com/blog/ja/products/serverless/cloud-run-gpus-are-now-generally-available"},{"title":"GPU support for services","url":"https://docs.cloud.google.com/run/docs/configuring/services/gpu?hl=en"},{"title":"GPU support for services","url":"https://docs.cloud.google.com/run/docs/configuring/services/gpu"},{"title":"GPU support for services","url":"https://docs.cloud.google.com/run/docs/configuring/services/gpu?authuser=1"},{"title":"GPU support for services","url":"https://docs.cloud.google.com/run/docs/configuring/services/gpu?authuser=0"},{"title":"GPU support for services","url":"https://docs.cloud.google.com/run/docs/configuring/services/gpu-zonal-redundancy?authuser=2"},{"title":"GPU support for worker pools","url":"https://docs.cloud.google.com/run/docs/configuring/workerpools/gpu"},{"title":"Configure GPUs for Cloud Run jobs","url":"https://docs.cloud.google.com/run/docs/configuring/jobs/gpu"}]},"The search confirmed GA for Cloud Run GPUs on NVIDIA L4 but did not return the actual price figures.\n\n- **GA status:** Google's GA announcement says the L4 is open to all customers without a quota request, and GPU support is now covered by the Cloud Run SLA (Cloud Run GPUs are now available to everyone for NVIDIA L4 GPUs, with no quota request required). Coverage now extends to the SLA, which is a change from the earlier preview period.\n- **Enabling it:** Setup is a single flag or checkbox, simply use --gpu 1 from the Cloud Run command line, or check the \"GPU\" checkbox in the console.\n- **Pricing levers:** Zonal redundancy is on by default. Turning it off gives a lower rate in exchange for best-effort failover during a zonal outage (you can turn off zonal redundancy and benefit from a lower price for best-effort failover of your GPU workloads). Billing is per-instance and you must use instance-based billing to use the GPU feature, minimum instances are charged at the full rate even when idle.\n- **Regions:** Five regions were listed at GA: us-central1, europe-west1, europe-west4, asia-southeast1, and asia-south1. The current docs also list us-east4 and mark some regions as invitation-only or quota-dependent, so check the docs for your target region.\n- **Quota:** New projects get a small default allotment. Projects using Cloud Run nvidia-l4 GPUs in a region for the first time are automatically granted 3 GPU quota (zonal redundancy off) when the first deployment is created. Additional GPUs require a quota increase request.\n- **Newer hardware:** The current docs also list an NVIDIA RTX PRO 6000 Blackwell option, which is still in Preview.\n- **Pricing gap:** None of the results gave the per-second L4 rates. A commenter noted that third-party providers such as Runpod can have hourly rates for L4, A100, and H100 GPUs can be significantly lower than Google's, even when considering Google's per-second billing. For exact figures, use the Cloud Run pricing page, which the GPU docs point to for GPU rates. A follow-up search aimed at that page would be the next step."],"durationSeconds":7.3813958749994635,"searchCount":1},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"215e8835-f7cb-4d6b-b165-abd3903573b5","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"session_id":"e8fe1454-894d-486c-ada2-536b95330a4e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/anchildress1/git_personal/gravespeaker","sessionId":"a78fbb29-c412-483a-b679-0722adb27f13","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"test/benchmark-fixtures"}
