{"parentUuid":"9caa28c2-b41e-4077-933a-a0b21f7d2c63","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"PreToolUse:WebSearch","toolUseID":"toolu_01FrMgjyfLEsG9SkZEPmJPud","hookEvent":"PreToolUse","content":"","stdout":"{}\n","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"python3 \"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/hooks/pretooluse.py\"","durationMs":54},"type":"attachment","uuid":"24ec536b-1911-42a1-9d35-5fa1bfb79fbd","timestamp":"2026-10-27T18:18:23.075Z","session_id":"e8fe1454-894d-486c-ada2-536b95330a4e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/anchildress1/git_personal/gravespeaker","sessionId":"a78fbb29-c412-483a-b679-0722adb27f13","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"test/benchmark-fixtures"}
{"parentUuid":"5184641c-4069-4ff3-b62f-00ae328e453f","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"35537cc9-ba97-458d-9db8-2b66ba5461e6","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FrMgjyfLEsG9SkZEPmJPud","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Gemini API pricing Gemma models free of charge paid tier\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"ai.google.dev\",\"url\":\"https://ai.google.dev/pricing?hl=fi\"},{\"title\":\"Gemini API Pricing\",\"url\":\"https://developer.puter.com/tutorials/gemini-api-pricing/\"},{\"title\":\"ai.google.dev\",\"url\":\"https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/pricing?authuser=3\"},{\"title\":\"ai.google.dev\",\"url\":\"https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/pricing?authuser=6\"},{\"title\":\"Gemini API Free Tier in 2026: Limits, Models, and When You Get Billed\",\"url\":\"https://apidog.com/blog/gemini-api-free-tier/\"},{\"title\":\"ai.google.dev\",\"url\":\"https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/billing?authuser=1\"},{\"title\":\"ai.google.dev\",\"url\":\"https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/billing?authuser=9\"},{\"title\":\"Gemini API\",\"url\":\"https://flexprice.io/pricing-index/google-gemini-api\"},{\"title\":\"Introduction to Google Gemini\",\"url\":\"https://metacto.com/blogs/the-true-cost-of-google-gemini-a-guide-to-api-pricing-and-integration\"}]\n\nGemma models are free-tier only in the sources I found, and the most recent ones say Gemma 4 is free on the Gemini API. The official Google pricing pages in the results are older cached versions.\n\n- **Gemma 3 (older Google pricing page):** Free-tier input and output are free of charge, and the paid tier is not available for Gemma 3. Gemma 3 free tier input price is free of charge, paid tier not available\n- **Gemma 4 (recent third-party summaries):** One page lists Gemma 4 (open) as free on the free tier only. An October 2026 Apidog guide says the free tier still covers Gemma 4 and several audio and embedding models for $0, with no billing account.\n- **How the free tier works:** Google describes it as offered through the API service with lower rate limits for testing purposes. Google AI Studio usage is completely free in all available countries. The paid tier brings higher rate limits, additional features, and different data handling.\n- **Data use:** Google uses free-tier prompts and responses to improve its products, and paid-tier ones it doesn't.\n- **Switching to paid:** To transition from the Free tier to a paid tier, you must first enable Cloud Billing for your Google Cloud project.\n\nCaveat: the Apidog and puter.com pages are newer, but they are secondary sources. I didn't confirm Gemma 4's status on Google's own current pricing page, so check that page before relying on it.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"fa3240cc-9213-4dd1-be04-83399934ac30","timestamp":"2026-10-27T18:18:29.966Z","toolUseResult":{"query":"Gemini API pricing Gemma models free of charge paid tier","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01B9JH4HykmArEVrsMqdvypQ","content":[{"title":"ai.google.dev","url":"https://ai.google.dev/pricing?hl=fi"},{"title":"Gemini API Pricing","url":"https://developer.puter.com/tutorials/gemini-api-pricing/"},{"title":"ai.google.dev","url":"https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/pricing?authuser=3"},{"title":"ai.google.dev","url":"https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/pricing?authuser=6"},{"title":"Gemini API Free Tier in 2026: Limits, Models, and When You Get Billed","url":"https://apidog.com/blog/gemini-api-free-tier/"},{"title":"ai.google.dev","url":"https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/billing?authuser=1"},{"title":"ai.google.dev","url":"https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/billing?authuser=9"},{"title":"Gemini API","url":"https://flexprice.io/pricing-index/google-gemini-api"},{"title":"Introduction to Google Gemini","url":"https://metacto.com/blogs/the-true-cost-of-google-gemini-a-guide-to-api-pricing-and-integration"}]},"Gemma models are free-tier only in the sources I found, and the most recent ones say Gemma 4 is free on the Gemini API. The official Google pricing pages in the results are older cached versions.\n\n- **Gemma 3 (older Google pricing page):** Free-tier input and output are free of charge, and the paid tier is not available for Gemma 3. Gemma 3 free tier input price is free of charge, paid tier not available\n- **Gemma 4 (recent third-party summaries):** One page lists Gemma 4 (open) as free on the free tier only. An October 2026 Apidog guide says the free tier still covers Gemma 4 and several audio and embedding models for $0, with no billing account.\n- **How the free tier works:** Google describes it as offered through the API service with lower rate limits for testing purposes. Google AI Studio usage is completely free in all available countries. The paid tier brings higher rate limits, additional features, and different data handling.\n- **Data use:** Google uses free-tier prompts and responses to improve its products, and paid-tier ones it doesn't.\n- **Switching to paid:** To transition from the Free tier to a paid tier, you must first enable Cloud Billing for your Google Cloud project.\n\nCaveat: the Apidog and puter.com pages are newer, but they are secondary sources. I didn't confirm Gemma 4's status on Google's own current pricing page, so check that page before relying on it."],"durationSeconds":6.8529579159999265,"searchCount":1},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"5184641c-4069-4ff3-b62f-00ae328e453f","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"session_id":"e8fe1454-894d-486c-ada2-536b95330a4e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/anchildress1/git_personal/gravespeaker","sessionId":"a78fbb29-c412-483a-b679-0722adb27f13","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"test/benchmark-fixtures"}
