{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"a78fbb29-c412-483a-b679-0722adb27f13","hash":"bc7df03ada01c016172fb31b691cb92934b553cde27b94ea1247d85093a6be0c","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_011wdbjvGnyBareQVP5ALSdA","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/anchildress1/git_personal/gravespeaker && set -a && . ./.env && set +a && curl -s \"https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta/models?pageSize=1000\" -H \"x-goog-api-key: $GEMINI_API_KEY\" | python3 -I -c 'import json,sys;[print(m[\"name\"],\"|\",m.get(\"displayName\")) for m in json.load(sys.stdin)[\"models\"] if \"gemma\" in m[\"name\"]]'; which ollama llama-server 2>&1 | head -2; sysctl -n hw.memsize machdep.cpu.brand_string","description":"List all hosted Gemma models and check local inference capacity"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01DhGTtinwiqPKsvBUugBVVa","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"Gemma 4 model sizes E2B E4B 26B A4B 31B release","mode":"standard"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01A97y7rBadYJzmWBCcMX41j","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"Cloud Run GPU support NVIDIA L4 general availability pricing","mode":"standard"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01FrMgjyfLEsG9SkZEPmJPud","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"Gemini API pricing Gemma models free of charge paid tier","mode":"standard"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01UM2KcHcpX5gHgR5yZiveY4","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"Render GPU instances support 2026; DigitalOcean GPU Droplets serverless inference Gemma","mode":"standard"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"a78fbb29-c412-483a-b679-0722adb27f13","hash":"84ba55f6694d008690fd8fd07abf857bd664eadbe586c4fa3642127e879836b4","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011wdbjvGnyBareQVP5ALSdA","type":"tool_result","content":"models/gemma-4-26b-a4b-it | Gemma 4 26B A4B IT\nmodels/gemma-4-31b-it | Gemma 4 31B IT\n/usr/local/bin/ollama\n/opt/homebrew/bin/llama-server\n38654705664\nApple M4 Max","is_error":false},{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DhGTtinwiqPKsvBUugBVVa","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Gemma 4 model sizes E2B E4B 26B A4B 31B release\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Google Releases Gemma 4: Frontier Open Models Under Apache 2.0\",\"url\":\"https://rits.shanghai.nyu.edu/ai/google-releases-gemma-4-frontier-open-models-under-apache-2-0/\"},{\"title\":\"ai.google.dev\",\"url\":\"https://ai.google.dev/gemma/docs/releases?hl=en\"},{\"title\":\"www.issoh.co.jp\",\"url\":\"https://www.issoh.co.jp/tech/details/11651/\"},{\"title\":\"Simon Willison’s Weblog\",\"url\":\"https://simonwillison.net/b/9404\"},{\"title\":\"本頁面記錄 Gemma 系列模型的版本。\",\"url\":\"https://ai.google.dev/gemma/docs/releases?hl=zh-TW\"},{\"title\":\"ai.google.dev\",\"url\":\"https://ai.google.dev/gemma/docs/core\"},{\"title\":\"gemma 4\",\"url\":\"https://ai.google.dev/edge/litert-lm/models/gemma-4\"},{\"title\":\"Claude Market Blog\",\"url\":\"https://claudemarket.ai/blog/gemma-4-google-open-model\"},{\"title\":\"ai.google.dev\",\"url\":\"https://ai.google.dev/gemma/docs/releases?hl=it\"}]\n\nThe search turned up the original Gemma 4 lineup and a later addition, which you should know about because your query didn't include it.\n\n- **Original launch (March 31 to April 2, 2026):** The family came in four sizes: E2B and E4B for edge devices, plus a 26B mixture-of-experts model and a 31B dense model. E2B has 2.3B effective parameters, E4B has 4.5B effective, 26B A4B has 26B total with 3.8B active, and 31B Dense has 30.7B parameters. Google's release log dates the launch to March 31, 2026, while a secondary source gives April 2 for the public announcement.\n- **Context and features:** The edge models have 128K context and native audio input, and the two larger models have 256K context. Video processing is supported across the family.\n- **Later additions:** Google's release page lists Gemma 4 - MTP for E2B, E4B, 31B, and 26B A4B on April 16, 2026, and Gemma 4 12B Unified on June 3, 2026. The developer docs describe the 12B as a 12B parameter encoder free model for multimodal tasks, which makes five sizes in total. Only the four original sizes appear in the other sources I found, so the 12B's details are less well confirmed.\n- **Naming note:** One Japanese guide lists the 26B MoE as 25.2B total parameters with 3.8B active, which conflicts with the 26B figure in the other sources.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."},{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UM2KcHcpX5gHgR5yZiveY4","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Render GPU instances support 2026; DigitalOcean GPU Droplets serverless inference Gemma\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"2026'da Render İçin En İyi 8 GPU (İnceleme ve Kıyas)\",\"url\":\"https://www.myarchitectai.com/tr/blog/best-gpu-for-rendering\"},{\"title\":\"gpu ai render trends 2026 neural rendering render farms\",\"url\":\"https://superrendersfarm.com/es/article/gpu-ai-render-trends-2026-neural-rendering-render-farms\"},{\"title\":\"gpu ai render trends 2026 neural rendering render farms\",\"url\":\"https://superrendersfarm.com/pt-pt/article/gpu-ai-render-trends-2026-neural-rendering-render-farms\"},{\"title\":\"gpu ai render trends 2026 neural rendering render farms\",\"url\":\"https://superrendersfarm.com/it/article/gpu-ai-render-trends-2026-neural-rendering-render-farms\"},{\"title\":\"gpu ai render trends 2026 neural rendering render farms\",\"url\":\"https://superrendersfarm.com/article/gpu-ai-render-trends-2026-neural-rendering-render-farms\"},{\"title\":\"gpu ai render trends 2026 neural rendering render farms\",\"url\":\"https://superrendersfarm.com/fr/article/gpu-ai-render-trends-2026-neural-rendering-render-farms\"},{\"title\":\"gpu ai render trends 2026 neural rendering render farms\",\"url\":\"https://superrendersfarm.com/de/article/gpu-ai-render-trends-2026-neural-rendering-render-farms\"},{\"title\":\"gpu ai render trends 2026 neural rendering render farms\",\"url\":\"https://superrendersfarm.com/vi/article/gpu-ai-render-trends-2026-neural-rendering-render-farms\"},{\"title\":\"best gpu for 3d rendering 2026\",\"url\":\"https://superrendersfarm.com/vi/article/best-gpu-for-3d-rendering-2026\"}]\n\nThe search didn't return anything on Render's cloud GPU offering. Every result was about 3D rendering (GPU choice for Blender/V-Ray-style workloads, render farm trends), not Render the hosting platform, so I can't confirm its 2026 GPU instance support from these results.\n\nI didn't search the DigitalOcean GPU Droplets or Gemma inference part of your query, since you asked for a single search. I can run a separate search for either one. For Render, checking its official docs or pricing page would be the most reliable route.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."},{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01A97y7rBadYJzmWBCcMX41j","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Cloud Run GPU support NVIDIA L4 general availability pricing\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"google cloud run nvidia gpu\",\"url\":\"https://www.infoq.com/news/2025/06/google-cloud-run-nvidia-gpu\"},{\"title\":\"Jump to Content\",\"url\":\"https://cloud.google.com/blog/products/serverless/cloud-run-gpus-are-now-generally-available\"},{\"title\":\"cloud run gpus are now generally available\",\"url\":\"https://cloud.google.com/blog/ja/products/serverless/cloud-run-gpus-are-now-generally-available\"},{\"title\":\"GPU support for services\",\"url\":\"https://docs.cloud.google.com/run/docs/configuring/services/gpu?hl=en\"},{\"title\":\"GPU support for services\",\"url\":\"https://docs.cloud.google.com/run/docs/configuring/services/gpu\"},{\"title\":\"GPU support for services\",\"url\":\"https://docs.cloud.google.com/run/docs/configuring/services/gpu?authuser=1\"},{\"title\":\"GPU support for services\",\"url\":\"https://docs.cloud.google.com/run/docs/configuring/services/gpu?authuser=0\"},{\"title\":\"GPU support for services\",\"url\":\"https://docs.cloud.google.com/run/docs/configuring/services/gpu-zonal-redundancy?authuser=2\"},{\"title\":\"GPU support for worker pools\",\"url\":\"https://docs.cloud.google.com/run/docs/configuring/workerpools/gpu\"},{\"title\":\"Configure GPUs for Cloud Run jobs\",\"url\":\"https://docs.cloud.google.com/run/docs/configuring/jobs/gpu\"}]\n\nThe search confirmed GA for Cloud Run GPUs on NVIDIA L4 but did not return the actual price figures.\n\n- **GA status:** Google's GA announcement says the L4 is open to all customers without a quota request, and GPU support is now covered by the Cloud Run SLA (Cloud Run GPUs are now available to everyone for NVIDIA L4 GPUs, with no quota request required). Coverage now extends to the SLA, which is a change from the earlier preview period.\n- **Enabling it:** Setup is a single flag or checkbox, simply use --gpu 1 from the Cloud Run command line, or check the \"GPU\" checkbox in the console.\n- **Pricing levers:** Zonal redundancy is on by default. Turning it off gives a lower rate in exchange for best-effort failover during a zonal outage (you can turn off zonal redundancy and benefit from a lower price for best-effort failover of your GPU workloads). Billing is per-instance and you must use instance-based billing to use the GPU feature, minimum instances are charged at the full rate even when idle.\n- **Regions:** Five regions were listed at GA: us-central1, europe-west1, europe-west4, asia-southeast1, and asia-south1. The current docs also list us-east4 and mark some regions as invitation-only or quota-dependent, so check the docs for your target region.\n- **Quota:** New projects get a small default allotment. Projects using Cloud Run nvidia-l4 GPUs in a region for the first time are automatically granted 3 GPU quota (zonal redundancy off) when the first deployment is created. Additional GPUs require a quota increase request.\n- **Newer hardware:** The current docs also list an NVIDIA RTX PRO 6000 Blackwell option, which is still in Preview.\n- **Pricing gap:** None of the results gave the per-second L4 rates. A commenter noted that third-party providers such as Runpod can have hourly rates for L4, A100, and H100 GPUs can be significantly lower than Google's, even when considering Google's per-second billing. For exact figures, use the Cloud Run pricing page, which the GPU docs point to for GPU rates. A follow-up search aimed at that page would be the next step.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."},{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FrMgjyfLEsG9SkZEPmJPud","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Gemini API pricing Gemma models free of charge paid tier\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"ai.google.dev\",\"url\":\"https://ai.google.dev/pricing?hl=fi\"},{\"title\":\"Gemini API Pricing\",\"url\":\"https://developer.puter.com/tutorials/gemini-api-pricing/\"},{\"title\":\"ai.google.dev\",\"url\":\"https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/pricing?authuser=3\"},{\"title\":\"ai.google.dev\",\"url\":\"https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/pricing?authuser=6\"},{\"title\":\"Gemini API Free Tier in 2026: Limits, Models, and When You Get Billed\",\"url\":\"https://apidog.com/blog/gemini-api-free-tier/\"},{\"title\":\"ai.google.dev\",\"url\":\"https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/billing?authuser=1\"},{\"title\":\"ai.google.dev\",\"url\":\"https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/billing?authuser=9\"},{\"title\":\"Gemini API\",\"url\":\"https://flexprice.io/pricing-index/google-gemini-api\"},{\"title\":\"Introduction to Google Gemini\",\"url\":\"https://metacto.com/blogs/the-true-cost-of-google-gemini-a-guide-to-api-pricing-and-integration\"}]\n\nGemma models are free-tier only in the sources I found, and the most recent ones say Gemma 4 is free on the Gemini API. The official Google pricing pages in the results are older cached versions.\n\n- **Gemma 3 (older Google pricing page):** Free-tier input and output are free of charge, and the paid tier is not available for Gemma 3. Gemma 3 free tier input price is free of charge, paid tier not available\n- **Gemma 4 (recent third-party summaries):** One page lists Gemma 4 (open) as free on the free tier only. An October 2026 Apidog guide says the free tier still covers Gemma 4 and several audio and embedding models for $0, with no billing account.\n- **How the free tier works:** Google describes it as offered through the API service with lower rate limits for testing purposes. Google AI Studio usage is completely free in all available countries. The paid tier brings higher rate limits, additional features, and different data handling.\n- **Data use:** Google uses free-tier prompts and responses to improve its products, and paid-tier ones it doesn't.\n- **Switching to paid:** To transition from the Free tier to a paid tier, you must first enable Cloud Billing for your Google Cloud project.\n\nCaveat: the Apidog and puter.com pages are newer, but they are secondary sources. I didn't confirm Gemma 4's status on Google's own current pricing page, so check that page before relying on it.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]}}
