{"parentUuid":"03893b80-3112-4dbe-9da6-bcac918de9b8","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"35537cc9-ba97-458d-9db8-2b66ba5461e6","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\n<system-reminder>\n<tools-used-before-summary>Artifact, ArtifactData, Bash, Edit, Read, Skill, ToolSearch, WebFetch, WebSearch, Write</tools-used-before-summary>\n</system-reminder>\nSummary:\n## 1. Primary Request and Intent\n\n**Project:** Gravespeaker, an MVP for Hacktoberfest 2026 \"Ghost in the Machine\". Hard deadline: 2026-10-31 23:59 PDT. Today is 2026-10-27.\n- User flow: photograph a headstone → AI extracts fields → search records with SerpApi → user confirms identity → grounded first-person narrative with citations.\n- Repo: `/Users/anchildress1/git_personal/gravespeaker`. SvelteKit, Node 26.12.1, pnpm 11.28.9, Mastra, Gemma 4 through the Gemini API, Cloud Run deploy.\n\n**Requests over the session:**\n1. Start a new branch, install spec-kit (used going forward), and plan the build.\n   - Add a v2 PRD entry for searching socials for people who died after a cutoff year, via SerpApi, grounded in a search.\n   - That branch is spec-kit setup only. Feature builds go on new branches.\n2. Prettier config fix (approved).\n   - Pick the cutoff year: user accepted 2010.\n   - Get fixture headstones.\n   - Update CLAUDE.md for minimal output.\n3. Disallow famous people in fixtures.\n4. Find a pre-1900 illegible stone; set cutoff 2010; make atomic commits as you go; add `.semgrepignore`; remove `archbald-tomb`; focus on modern graves.\n5. Too many images. Focus is modern, meaning post-2010, graves. Set up an easy human review of the answer key.\n6. Manifest must hold the full stone text: `notes` becomes `text`, `people` unchanged.\n   - Fix history (fine if not pushed; only ask after pushing to GitHub).\n   - Delete dead code and config.\n7. Holmquist is an edge case to test. User then corrected me: they never said to exclude it from scoring.\n8. \"run the benchmark now\".\n9. **LATEST (in progress), verbatim:**\n   - \"make sure these results are stored in a file somewhere for reference during the post.\"\n   - \"note: the code must use mastra properly to retry as needed and handle errors. this is a given anyway\"\n   - \"holmquist which was a dual tombstone is now a non-goal. add TTD for v2 to the PRD that says we can tune the prompts then for that scenario\"\n   - \"take that one out and gemma 4 26b works and is hosted. is there a smaller hosted gemma? Cloud Run doesn't give me GPUs. Could we use render or digital ocean? if yes, test smaller gemma locally. this kills our open model requirement if flash is honestly that much better. only diff is that open ones are free with gemini key?? ground in a search.\"\n   - \"we need a deterministic layer in the code that parses names, strips/normalizes dates.\"\n   - \"languages other than english are also a non-goal for now, do not code against but we will not optimize for them\"\n\n## 2. Key Technical Concepts\n\n- **GitHub spec-kit v1.2.3**, installed via `uvx --from git+https://github.com/github/spec-kit.git@v1.2.3 specify init --here --force --integration claude --script sh --non-interactive --ignore-agent-tools`. Skills: `/speckit-specify` → `/speckit-plan` → `/speckit-tasks` → `/speckit-implement`.\n- **Gemini API models available with the project key:**\n  - Hosted Gemma: only `gemma-4-26b-a4b-it` and `gemma-4-31b-it`. No smaller hosted Gemma.\n  - Closed comparison model: `gemini-3.8-flash`.\n- **Gemma 4 family:** E2B, E4B, 26B A4B (3.8B active), 31B dense, and 12B Unified (added June 2026).\n- **Pricing (official page, fetched):**\n  - Gemma 4: free tier \"Free of charge\"; paid tier \"Not available\". So production runs on free-tier rate limits, and Google uses free-tier data to improve its products.\n  - gemini-3.8-flash paid: $0.75 input / $3.75 output per 1M tokens through 2026-12-31.\n- **Cloud Run DOES support GPUs:** NVIDIA L4 is GA with no quota request and 3 GPUs auto-granted. This contradicts the user's premise and must be pushed back on.\n- **Render / DigitalOcean:** the search returned nothing usable.\n- **Local hardware:** Apple M4 Max with 36 GB. Ollama 0.40.11 already has `gemma4:26b` and `gemma4:12b`; `llama-server` is also installed.\n- **SerpApi:**\n  - Google engine supports the `site:` operator.\n  - Facebook Profile API needs `profile_id` (no name search).\n  - An Instagram Profile engine exists. No LinkedIn engine.\n- **Wikimedia Commons:** API used for CC-licensed fixtures; Wikipedia API used for notability checks.\n- **Artifact** with `db` + `user` capabilities, used for the review page.\n\n## 3. Files and Code Sections\n\n**Branch `chore/speckit-setup`** (unpushed):\n- `e4bcc9e` build: install GitHub spec-kit 1.2.3 with the Claude integration. Adds `.claude/skills/speckit-*`, `.specify/`, and `/.specify/` in `.prettierignore` (its manifests hash the generated files).\n- `57c2b57` docs: ratify the Gravespeaker spec-kit constitution (`.specify/memory/constitution.md`).\n  - Gates: MVP scope, never fabricate history, never silently merge identities, two seams only, behavior-driven tests.\n  - Defers to CLAUDE.md and the PRD.\n- `e346e3a` docs: limit agent output to what the user must act on. Adds a `## Output` section to CLAUDE.md:\n  ```\n  ## Output\n  - The user designs; you implement. Report only what the user must act on or must know changed in the repo.\n  - Per change: file and one-line effect. No narration of steps, tools, or reasoning.\n  - Surface blockers, decisions needed, and failures in full. Omit everything else.\n  ```\n- `a1e8487` docs: add social media search for recent deaths to the v2 PRD. PRD §10 entry \"Social media search for recent deaths (key v2 feature)\":\n  - Death year 2010 or later.\n  - Pew stat: social networking among online adults 50+ reached 42% in 2010.\n  - SerpApi two-step: Google `site:` search, then the Facebook/Instagram profile engines.\n  - No LinkedIn engine.\n  - Profile hits go through normal identity verification.\n  - Living people's details stay out; link, don't republish.\n\n**Branch `test/benchmark-fixtures`** (current; from main; unpushed; history rewritten cleanly):\n- `c1cc170` test: add 9 headstone fixtures with ground truth for the benchmark.\n- `2810dd1` docs: set fixture rules for the headstone benchmark. CLAUDE.md Layout lines:\n  ```\n  - Benchmark script: `scripts/benchmark.ts`. Fixture images: `fixtures/`, ground truth in `fixtures/manifest.json`.\n  - Fixtures never depict notable people (anyone with a Wikipedia article). Models already know them, which inflates OCR and grounding scores. Same-name namesakes are allowed and noted as identity traps.\n  - Keep the fixture set small. Recent graves (death 2010+) are the baseline. Historic stones are a minority that stress-test reading, never the norm.\n  - Ground truth is unverified until the user reviews it (`reviewed: true`). Never publish benchmark numbers from unreviewed fixtures.\n  ```\n  This branch's CLAUDE.md does NOT have the Output section; that lives on the other branch.\n- `0a2fb9b` build: keep benchmark fixtures out of the Docker build context. Adds `fixtures` to `.dockerignore`.\n- `138e1a1` chore: drop gitignore entries for hosts and files this repo never uses. Removes `.output .vercel .netlify .wrangler` and `!.env.test`.\n- `60e756e` test: mark the headstone answer key as human-reviewed.\n  - User's own edits: all `reviewed: true`; Ellis text corrected to \"Tho,s\" and \"aged 11 years\".\n  - Trailer: `Commit-generated-by`.\n\n**`fixtures/manifest.json`** schema per entry:\n```\n{ file, era: \"recent\"|\"historic\", difficulty: \"clean\"|\"weathered\"|\"edge\"|\"illegible\", text: string|null (lines joined by \\n, [?] for unreadable word), people: [{name, born, died}] (dates \"YYYY\" or \"YYYY-MM-DD\", ? for unreadable digit, null if absent), source, author, license, licenseUrl, reviewed }\n```\n\n**Fixtures (9):**\n| File | Expected people | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| chambers-2011 | Corwin \"Cory\" Garner Chambers, 1959-11-07 to 2011-09-12 | |\n| gonzalez-2021 | Alfonso Gonzalez, 1951-11-18 to 2021-01-17 | Spanish |\n| guo-2025 | Jiunn-Shih Guo, 1937-01-18 to 2025-12-10 | Chinese 郭俊士 |\n| hildebrand-iii-2018 | Edward Hildebrand III, 1966 to 2018 | |\n| hildebrand-jr-2015 | Edward Leroy Hildebrand Jr, 1942-04-28 to 2015-10-10 | |\n| holmquist-2024 | Marsha Fox Holmquist, b. 1940-11-05; Charles Ray Holmquist, 1948-03-12 to 2024-05-06 | |\n| cunningham-1752 | Andrew Cunningham, d. 1752-04-27 | |\n| ellis-1818 | Betsey Ellis, d. 1818-07-28 | Zoom confirmed 1818 |\n| illegible-marble | none | text null |\n\n**Benchmark scratch scripts** (not in repo), in `/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-anchildress1-git-personal-gravespeaker/a78fbb29-c412-483a-b679-0722adb27f13/scratchpad/bench/`:\n- `run.mjs`: REST `generateContent` via fetch, temperature 0, same PROMPT for all models, `AbortSignal.timeout(240_000)`, writes results after each call. Scores text by Levenshtein-normalized similarity; people by name match plus born/died.\n- `results.json`: the full hosted run.\n- `run-local.mjs`: Ollama `/api/chat` variant (`think: false`, images base64). Models come from the `MODELS` env var; holmquist excluded.\n- `results-local-12b.json`.\n- PROMPT (verbatim core):\n  ```\n  You are reading a photo of a gravestone for a historical research tool.\n  Transcribe ONLY what is carved or cast on the stone. Do NOT add, guess, or complete anything you cannot see.\n  Return ONLY a JSON object, no prose, no code fences:\n  {\"text\": string|null, \"people\": [{\"name\": string, \"born\": string|null, \"died\": string|null}]}\n  - text: every line of the inscription in order, joined with \"\\n\". Write \"[?]\" for a word you cannot read. null if nothing is legible.\n  - people: one entry per person commemorated. name exactly as carved. born/died as \"YYYY\" or \"YYYY-MM-DD\"; use \"?\" for an unreadable digit; null when the date is not on the stone. [] if no name is legible.\n  - A year that is not a birth or death (marriage length, erection date) is NOT a life date.\n  ```\n- **Rescoring logic** (Python, run inline): name tokens lowercased with non `[a-z0-9 ]` stripped (this drops CJK), \"m.r\" mapped to \"mr\", honorifics `mr/mrs/miss/dr` removed; tokens must match exactly. A person whose name doesn't match gets 0 for all three fields.\n\n**Review artifact:** https://claude.ai/artifact/2xtJSGENbbvQBMcHxyGKsZ\n- Source: `/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-anchildress1-git-personal-gravespeaker/a78fbb29-c412-483a-b679-0722adb27f13/scratchpad/review/index.html`.\n- Uses `db` collection `reviews`, which is empty. The user reviewed in the IDE instead, so the page is obsolete; I offered deletion with no answer.\n\n## 4. Errors and fixes\n\n- **`specify init --here` refused a non-empty dir under `--non-interactive`:** added `--force`, after a scratch dry run confirmed it only writes `.claude/skills` and `.specify`.\n- **Prettier failed on `.specify` files:** added `/.specify/` to `.prettierignore` with user approval. Reformatting would break spec-kit's manifest hashes.\n- **Semgrep Guardian \"payload exceeded maximum size\":** Guardian scans files touched by tool calls (the JPGs) and ignores `.semgrepignore`. Nothing in the repo runs Semgrep, so `.semgrepignore` was dead and was removed during the history rewrite.\n- **Famous people in fixtures** (side-agent note; user said fix it): replaced with non-notables, checked via the Wikipedia API.\n- **Too many and too-old fixtures** (user feedback twice): trimmed to 9, post-2010 baseline.\n- **Answer key written by AI** (side agent): built the review page. The user reviewed in the manifest directly.\n- **`notes` → `text`:** user wanted the full inscription; replaced.\n- **Commit bullet wrap** in an old commit: resolved by the history rewrite.\n- **User correction:** I added `scored: false` for holmquist and a CLAUDE.md rule. User: \"I did not say to skip it in scoring. what i said was test it and if it doesn't work then we'll adjust the requirements\". Dropped that commit with `git reset --hard HEAD~1`; branch was unpushed and the tree clean.\n- **First benchmark run crashed:** `UND_ERR_HEADERS_TIMEOUT` from undici's 300 s default on a Gemma call, with no results saved. Added a per-call `AbortSignal.timeout(240_000)` with try/catch and incremental `writeFile`.\n- **Scoring too strict:** name compare was case-sensitive (models return CAPS). Rescored with normalized tokens.\n\n## 5. Problem Solving — benchmark results\n\n**Hosted run, all 9 fixtures (rescored):**\n| Model | Fields correct | Text similarity | Avg time | Timeouts |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| gemma-4-26b-a4b-it | 21/28 (75%) | 0.946 | 34.7 s | 0 |\n| gemma-4-31b-it | 18/25 (72%) | 0.941 | 55.0 s | 1 (cunningham) |\n| gemini-3.8-flash | 24/28 (86%) | 0.943 | 14.5 s | 0 |\n\n**Per-fixture findings:**\n- Holmquist: both Gemma models read every date right but left off the shared surname (0/6). Gemini scored 6/6.\n- Ellis: all three models read 1818 as 1848. Zoom confirmed 1818.\n- Gemini wrote \"LE ROY\" for LEROY on hildebrand-jr (0/3 under strict scoring; dates were right).\n\n**Excluding holmquist (not yet stated to the user):**\n- Gemma 26B: 21/22 (95%).\n- Gemma 31B: 18/19.\n- Gemini Flash: 18/22 (82%).\n- So Flash is NOT better; Gemma 26B leads. Speed is Gemma's only drawback. This contradicts the user's \"this kills our open model requirement\" premise.\n\n**Local Gemma 4 12B via Ollama (holmquist excluded), raw strict-score output:**\n- chambers 2/3 (likely a case issue), gonzalez 3/3, guo 3/3, hildebrand-iii 3/3, hildebrand-jr 2/3 (likely case), cunningham 0/3 with 1 extra (likely the \"Mr\" honorific), ellis text 0.74 and 0/3 with 1 extra, illegible 1/1.\n- About 4 s per image on the M4 Max.\n- Not yet rescored with the normalized scorer.\n\n**Other state:**\n- `ollama pull gemma4:e4b` running in background (task b5yjg8svu).\n- Conflict to flag: CLAUDE.md Scope says \"No feature flags, plugin systems, config layers, caching, retries, queues, or i18n unless a broken user path demands it.\" The user now requires Mastra retries and error handling. Update CLAUDE.md to allow Mastra's built-in retry and error handling (no hand-rolled retries) and tell the user about the change.\n\n## 6. All user messages\n\n1. \"Start a new branch. install speckit in this repo, we will use that going forward. read @docs/PRD.md and @CLAUDE.md. we need a plan of attack to actually accomplish this build in what little time we have to do it. Add to v2 PRD that we want to search socials for any person who died after XX year, which we will pick in addition to the gh search. This should be key feature and doable with SERPAPI. confirm with a grounded search. this branch will be speckit setup and init. feature builds will be on a new branch\"\n2. \"- yes to config for prettier. fix it. - help me pick a year that makes sense for the cutoff. - go get fixture headstones. we need to start there. i don't have time to find a cemetary rn. we can use good headstone pics, too. it should be a mix. - also update @CLAUDE.md to minimize output verbosity scoped only to what user needs to act on or needs to know about changes in the repo. the user designs. you code/implement.\"\n3. (Side-agent note about famous fixtures) \"fix this by disallowing famous people in the fixture for testing\"\n4. \"- search for early 19th century tombstone pics for can't read one - 2010 died after is fine - make atomic commits as you go - add semgrep ignore as suggested - archbald-tomb needs to go. too complex. - you also have all old and really old tombs. those are going to be hard to find and are the exception we need to test for reading markers, not the baseline for how the app functions. we're shooting for modern graves that must be present in the fixture test. keep the best old ones, some legible some not, but focus on modern\"\n5. \"this seems like a fuck ton of images for a \"small benchmark\" to see if gemma can read them cleanly like the PRD says. Especially when our focus is on modern aka post-2010 grave markers.\"\n6. (Mid-turn, after side-agent note about the AI-written answer key) \"we're going to fix this once I'm happy with the pics. you need to set this up so i can easily review. make corrections as needed or simply state illegible.\"\n7. \"now we're testing the ability of the llm to read the image, right? doesn't it make sense that you'd put in the manifest the full text from the gravestone? the llm also needs to pick the persons full name, birthdate, and deceased date. you've got these already. don't change it. notes should become full text though. - fix the history, fine if not pushed yet. you only have to ask after pushing to gh - delete dead code/config\"\n8. \"@fixtures/holmquist-2024.jpg this is an edge case. we'll run a test if the model can handle dual plots like this, but it is a non-goal if it cannot. we're not going to waste time on that. otherwise all are reviewed by me and marked true in manifest\"\n9. \"I did not say to skip it in scoring. what i said was test it and if it doesn't work then we'll adjust the requirements\"\n10. \"run the benchmark now\"\n11. (Latest) \"- make sure these results are stored in a file somewhere for reference during the post. - note: the code must use mastra properly to retry as needed and handle errors. this is a given anyway - holmquist which was a dual tombstone is now a non-goal. add TTD for v2 to the PRD that says we can tune the prompts then for that scenario - take that one out and gemma 4 26b works and is hosted. is there a smaller hosted gemma? Cloud Run doesn't give me GPUs. Could we use render or digital ocean? if yes, test smaller gemma locally. this kills our open model requirement if flash is honestly that much better. only diff is that open ones are free with gemini key?? ground in a search. - we need a deterministic layer in the code that parses names, strips/normalizes dates. - languages other than english are also a non-goal for now, do not code against but we will not optimize for them\"\n\n**Standing constraints, verbatim, from CLAUDE.md and the user's global rules:**\n- \"Never place secrets outside: a local `.env` file, or a secure vault explicitly chosen by the user.\"\n- \"Never print secret values. Pipe from `.env` into `gcloud secrets create --data-file=-`.\" (`.env` holds `GEMINI_API_KEY` and `SERPAPI_API_KEY`; loaded with `set -a && . ./.env`; never echo the values.)\n- \"Secret Manager bills per secret. Create one only when prod cannot run without it. Ask before adding any.\"\n- \"Never `git push` unless the user asks for it in that message.\"\n- \"All commits must be signed with a GPG key.\"\n- \"Commits never land directly on `main`.\"\n- \"Every AI-authored commit must include a `Generated-by` footer\"; commitlint also requires `Signed-off-by: Ashley Childress <anchildress1@gmail.com>`.\n- \"Never bypass Lefthook on commit or push: no `--no-verify`, no `LEFTHOOK=0`.\"\n- \"You may **not** modify repository configuration files unless explicitly instructed.\"\n- \"Never merge a release-please PR.\"\n- \"Lighthouse runs only through the chrome-devtools MCP ... Never add `@lhci/cli` or `lighthouse` to the repo.\"\n- \"Edit `README.md` only through the `readme-generator` skill.\"\n- \"Pin every GitHub Action ... to a full commit SHA.\"\n- \"Port kills: use `kill <pid>` only.\"\n- \"Mock at the network boundary (Gemini API, SerpApi). Never hit live APIs in tests.\"\n- \"Validation gate before reporting any change as done: `make ai-checks`.\"\n- History rewrites are OK before pushing; ask only after pushing to GitHub.\n- Use the generate-commit-message skill; atomic commits as you go.\n\n## 7. Pending Tasks (from the latest message)\n\n1. **Store the benchmark results in the repo** for the DEV post: e.g. `docs/benchmarks/` with a human-readable markdown summary plus the raw JSON (hosted + local). Commit.\n2. **Mastra retries and error handling:** record as a requirement and resolve the CLAUDE.md \"no retries\" conflict (Mastra built-in only, no hand-rolled). Flag the change to the user.\n3. **Holmquist / multi-person stones:**\n   - Mark as non-goal in the PRD.\n   - Add a v2 PRD entry (user wrote \"TTD\", read as TODO) to tune prompts for companion/dual stones then.\n   - \"take that one out\": remove `holmquist-2024` from fixtures and the manifest.\n4. **Answer the hosting questions, grounded:**\n   - No smaller hosted Gemma on the Gemini API (only 26B A4B and 31B).\n   - Cloud Run DOES have L4 GPUs (GA). Push back on the user's premise.\n   - Render / DigitalOcean: unverified, but unnecessary.\n   - Gemma 4 on the Gemini API is free-tier only; paid tier not available. Risks: rate limits and Google training on the data.\n   - Excluding holmquist, Gemma 26B 95% beats Flash 82%, so the open-model requirement survives; latency (~35 s vs ~15 s) is the real cost.\n   - PRD says no self-hosting unless benchmarks justify it.\n5. **Local smaller Gemma test:**\n   - Rescore the 12B results with the normalized scorer.\n   - Run E4B once the pull finishes: `MODELS=gemma4:e4b node $B/run-local.mjs \"$PWD/fixtures\" $B/results-local-e4b.json`.\n   - Report the comparison.\n6. **Deterministic layer for name parsing and date normalization:** record as a requirement (PRD/CLAUDE.md). Build it in the feature branch via spec-kit, not now.\n7. **Non-English languages:** add as a non-goal in the PRD (don't code against them; don't optimize for them).\n8. Still open: offer to delete the obsolete review artifact (no reply yet). `scripts/benchmark.ts` (the real Mastra-based benchmark) still needs building via spec-kit on a feature branch.\n\n## 8. Current Work\n\nWorking on the user's latest multi-part message:\n- Grounding searches are done:\n  - Gemma 4 sizes.\n  - Cloud Run GPU is GA.\n  - Pricing: Gemma 4 free-only, paid \"Not available\"; 3.8 Flash $0.75/$3.75.\n  - Render/DO search failed.\n- Hosted Gemma list confirmed: only 26b-a4b and 31b.\n- Local Ollama test of `gemma4:12b` ran on 8 fixtures (holmquist excluded) in about 4 s each; raw strict-score output is listed in section 5.\n- `ollama pull gemma4:e4b` was started in the background (task b5yjg8svu) and has not finished.\n- No repo edits yet for the latest message.\n- Current branch: `test/benchmark-fixtures`, clean, unpushed.\n\n## 9. Optional Next Step\n\nContinue the latest request: \"take that one out and gemma 4 26b works and is hosted. is there a smaller hosted gemma? ... if yes, test smaller gemma locally ... ground in a search.\"\n\n1. Rescore `results-local-12b.json` with the normalized scorer.\n2. When the E4B pull finishes, run `MODELS=gemma4:e4b node $B/run-local.mjs \"$PWD/fixtures\" $B/results-local-e4b.json` and rescore.\n3. Then, on `test/benchmark-fixtures`, with `make ai-checks` and one atomic signed commit per change:\n   - Remove the holmquist fixture.\n   - Write the results doc plus raw JSON under `docs/benchmarks/` (\"make sure these results are stored in a file somewhere for reference during the post\").\n   - Update the PRD: multi-person stones as non-goal plus v2 prompt-tuning TODO; non-English as non-goal; deterministic name/date normalization layer; Mastra retry/error handling.\n   - Update the CLAUDE.md retries line so Mastra built-in retries are allowed.\n4. Report the grounded hosting answer with source links:\n   - Cloud Run GPUs exist (https://cloud.google.com/blog/products/serverless/cloud-run-gpus-are-now-generally-available, https://docs.cloud.google.com/run/docs/configuring/services/gpu).\n   - Gemma 4 is free-tier only (https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/pricing).\n   - Gemma 4 sizes (https://ai.google.dev/gemma/docs/releases).\n   - Gemma 26B beats Flash once holmquist is excluded.\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /Users/anchildress1/.claude/projects/-Users-anchildress1-git-personal-gravespeaker/a78fbb29-c412-483a-b679-0722adb27f13.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened.\n\nThe messages after this summary are the most recent messages from before compaction, kept verbatim. The summary was written without seeing them, so something it says has not happened yet may already have happened in them."},"isVisibleInTranscriptOnly":true,"isCompactSummary":true,"uuid":"a1d974e4-375e-47f8-a628-70b828bf9c80","timestamp":"2026-10-27T18:21:36.983Z","turnPosition":{"promptIndex":10,"turnIndex":12},"turnOrigin":"human","summarizedTurnPromptUuids":["e189aa04-e378-4fa6-963f-1fced8a9e6a9"],"session_id":"e8fe1454-894d-486c-ada2-536b95330a4e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/anchildress1/git_personal/gravespeaker","sessionId":"a78fbb29-c412-483a-b679-0722adb27f13","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"test/benchmark-fixtures","slug":"shimmying-exploring-umbrella"}
{"parentUuid":"a1d974e4-375e-47f8-a628-70b828bf9c80","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"file","filename":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-anchildress1-git-personal-gravespeaker/a78fbb29-c412-483a-b679-0722adb27f13/scratchpad/bench/rescore.py","content":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-anchildress1-git-personal-gravespeaker/a78fbb29-c412-483a-b679-0722adb27f13/scratchpad/bench/rescore.py","content":"\"\"\"Rescore saved model answers: case/punctuation-insensitive names, honorifics and non-Latin script ignored.\"\"\"\nimport json, re, sys\nfrom collections import defaultdict\n\nmanifest = {e[\"file\"]: e for e in json.load(open(sys.argv[1]))}\nskip = set(sys.argv[2].split(\",\")) if sys.argv[2] else set()\nrows = [x for p in sys.argv[3:] for x in json.load(open(p)) if x[\"file\"] not in skip]\n\n\ndef toks(s):\n    t = re.sub(r\"[^a-z0-9 ]+\", \" \", (s or \"\").lower().replace(\"m.r\", \"mr\")).split()\n    return [x for x in t if x not in {\"mr\", \"mrs\", \"miss\", \"dr\"}]\n\n\nagg = defaultdict(lambda: defaultdict(float))\ncells = {}\nfor x in rows:\n    f, a = manifest[x[\"file\"]], agg[x[\"model\"]]\n    a[\"calls\"] += 1\n    a[\"ms\"] += x[\"ms\"]\n    if x.get(\"error\"):\n        a[\"errors\"] += 1\n        cells[(x[\"file\"], x[\"model\"])] = \"timeout\" if \"Timeout\" in x[\"error\"] else \"error\"\n        continue\n    a[\"text\"] += x[\"text\"]\n    got = list(x[\"got\"].get(\"people\") or [])\n    if not f[\"people\"]:\n        ok = 0 if got else 1\n        a[\"fields\"] += ok\n        a[\"total\"] += 1\n        cells[(x[\"file\"], x[\"model\"])] = f\"{ok}/1\"\n        continue\n    c = t = 0\n    for p in f[\"people\"]:\n        q = next((q for q in got if toks(q.get(\"name\")) == toks(p[\"name\"])), None)\n        if q:\n            got.remove(q)\n        for k in (\"name\", \"born\", \"died\"):\n            t += 1\n            c += bool(q) and (k == \"name\" or (q.get(k) or None) == (p[k] or None))\n    a[\"fields\"] += c\n    a[\"total\"] += t\n    cells[(x[\"file\"], x[\"model\"])] = f\"{c}/{t}\"\n\nmodels = list(agg)\nfiles = [fn for fn in manifest if fn not in skip]\nprint(\"| Fixture | \" + \" | \".join(models) + \" |\")\nprint(\"|---|\" + \"---|\" * len(models))\nfor fn in files:\n    print(f\"| {fn.removesuffix('.jpg')} | \" + \" | \".join(cells.get((fn, m), \"-\") for m in models) + \" |\")\nprint(\"| **Fields correct** | \" + \" | \".join(f\"**{int(a['fields'])}/{int(a['total'])} ({a['fields']/a['total']:.0%})**\" for a in agg.values()) + \" |\")\nprint(\"| Text similarity | \" + \" | \".join(f\"{a['text']/(a['calls']-a['errors']):.1%}\" for a in agg.values()) + \" |\")\nprint(\"| Timeouts | \" + \" | \".join(str(int(a[\"errors\"])) for a in agg.values()) + \" |\")\nprint(\"| Avg time per photo | \" + \" | \".join(f\"{a['ms']/a['calls']/1000:.1f} s\" for a in agg.values()) + \" |\")\n","numLines":55,"startLine":1,"totalLines":55}},"displayPath":"../../../../private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-anchildress1-git-personal-gravespeaker/a78fbb29-c412-483a-b679-0722adb27f13/scratchpad/bench/rescore.py"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"0e060ff2-1e14-4890-86da-59a19cf73c57","timestamp":"2026-10-27T18:21:37.310Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nCalled the Read tool with the following input: {\"file_path\":\"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-anchildress1-git-personal-gravespeaker/a78fbb29-c412-483a-b679-0722adb27f13/scratchpad/bench/rescore.py\"}\n</system-reminder>"},{"content":"<system-reminder>\nResult of calling the Read tool:\n1\t\"\"\"Rescore saved model answers: case/punctuation-insensitive names, honorifics and non-Latin script ignored.\"\"\"\n2\timport json, re, sys\n3\tfrom collections import defaultdict\n4\t\n5\tmanifest = {e[\"file\"]: e for e in json.load(open(sys.argv[1]))}\n6\tskip = set(sys.argv[2].split(\",\")) if sys.argv[2] else set()\n7\trows = [x for p in sys.argv[3:] for x in json.load(open(p)) if x[\"file\"] not in skip]\n8\t\n9\t\n10\tdef toks(s):\n11\t    t = re.sub(r\"[^a-z0-9 ]+\", \" \", (s or \"\").lower().replace(\"m.r\", \"mr\")).split()\n12\t    return [x for x in t if x not in {\"mr\", \"mrs\", \"miss\", \"dr\"}]\n13\t\n14\t\n15\tagg = defaultdict(lambda: defaultdict(float))\n16\tcells = {}\n17\tfor x in rows:\n18\t    f, a = manifest[x[\"file\"]], agg[x[\"model\"]]\n19\t    a[\"calls\"] += 1\n20\t    a[\"ms\"] += x[\"ms\"]\n21\t    if x.get(\"error\"):\n22\t        a[\"errors\"] += 1\n23\t        cells[(x[\"file\"], x[\"model\"])] = \"timeout\" if \"Timeout\" in x[\"error\"] else \"error\"\n24\t        continue\n25\t    a[\"text\"] += x[\"text\"]\n26\t    got = list(x[\"got\"].get(\"people\") or [])\n27\t    if not f[\"people\"]:\n28\t        ok = 0 if got else 1\n29\t        a[\"fields\"] += ok\n30\t        a[\"total\"] += 1\n31\t        cells[(x[\"file\"], x[\"model\"])] = f\"{ok}/1\"\n32\t        continue\n33\t    c = t = 0\n34\t    for p in f[\"people\"]:\n35\t        q = next((q for q in got if toks(q.get(\"name\")) == toks(p[\"name\"])), None)\n36\t        if q:\n37\t            got.remove(q)\n38\t        for k in (\"name\", \"born\", \"died\"):\n39\t            t += 1\n40\t            c += bool(q) and (k == \"name\" or (q.get(k) or None) == (p[k] or None))\n41\t    a[\"fields\"] += c\n42\t    a[\"total\"] += t\n43\t    cells[(x[\"file\"], x[\"model\"])] = f\"{c}/{t}\"\n44\t\n45\tmodels = list(agg)\n46\tfiles = [fn for fn in manifest if fn not in skip]\n47\tprint(\"| Fixture | \" + \" | \".join(models) + \" |\")\n48\tprint(\"|---|\" + \"---|\" * len(models))\n49\tfor fn in files:\n50\t    print(f\"| {fn.removesuffix('.jpg')} | \" + \" | \".join(cells.get((fn, m), \"-\") for m in models) + \" |\")\n51\tprint(\"| **Fields correct** | \" + \" | \".join(f\"**{int(a['fields'])}/{int(a['total'])} ({a['fields']/a['total']:.0%})**\" for a in agg.values()) + \" |\")\n52\tprint(\"| Text similarity | \" + \" | \".join(f\"{a['text']/(a['calls']-a['errors']):.1%}\" for a in agg.values()) + \" |\")\n53\tprint(\"| Timeouts | \" + \" | \".join(str(int(a[\"errors\"])) for a in agg.values()) + \" |\")\n54\tprint(\"| Avg time per photo | \" + \" | \".join(f\"{a['ms']/a['calls']/1000:.1f} s\" for a in agg.values()) + \" |\")\n55\t\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"e8fe1454-894d-486c-ada2-536b95330a4e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/anchildress1/git_personal/gravespeaker","sessionId":"a78fbb29-c412-483a-b679-0722adb27f13","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"test/benchmark-fixtures","slug":"shimmying-exploring-umbrella"}
{"parentUuid":"0e060ff2-1e14-4890-86da-59a19cf73c57","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"file","filename":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-anchildress1-git-personal-gravespeaker/a78fbb29-c412-483a-b679-0722adb27f13/scratchpad/bench/run.mjs","content":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-anchildress1-git-personal-gravespeaker/a78fbb29-c412-483a-b679-0722adb27f13/scratchpad/bench/run.mjs","content":"// Throwaway OCR smoke run: same prompt and images for every model, scored against fixtures/manifest.json.\nimport { readFile, writeFile } from \"node:fs/promises\";\n\nconst [fixturesDir, outFile] = process.argv.slice(2);\nconst KEY = process.env.GEMINI_API_KEY;\nconst MODELS = [\"gemma-4-26b-a4b-it\", \"gemma-4-31b-it\", \"gemini-3.8-flash\"];\n\nconst PROMPT = `You are reading a photo of a gravestone for a historical research tool.\n\nTranscribe ONLY what is carved or cast on the stone. Do NOT add, guess, or complete anything you cannot see.\n\nReturn ONLY a JSON object, no prose, no code fences:\n{\"text\": string|null, \"people\": [{\"name\": string, \"born\": string|null, \"died\": string|null}]}\n\n- text: every line of the inscription in order, joined with \"\\\\n\". Write \"[?]\" for a word you cannot read. null if nothing is legible.\n- people: one entry per person commemorated. name exactly as carved. born/died as \"YYYY\" or \"YYYY-MM-DD\"; use \"?\" for an unreadable digit; null when the date is not on the stone. [] if no name is legible.\n- A year that is not a birth or death (marriage length, erection date) is NOT a life date.`;\n\nconst norm = (s) => (s ?? \"\").toLowerCase().replace(/[^\\p{L}\\p{N}?]+/gu, \" \").trim();\n\nfunction lev(a, b) {\n  const d = Array.from({ length: a.length + 1 }, (_, i) => [i]);\n  for (let j = 1; j <= b.length; j++) d[0][j] = j;\n  for (let i = 1; i <= a.length; i++)\n    for (let j = 1; j <= b.length; j++)\n      d[i][j] = Math.min(d[i - 1][j] + 1, d[i][j - 1] + 1, d[i - 1][j - 1] + (a[i - 1] === b[j - 1] ? 0 : 1));\n  return d[a.length][b.length];\n}\n\nfunction textScore(expected, got) {\n  const e = norm(expected), g = norm(got);\n  if (!e) return g ? 0 : 1;\n  return Math.max(0, 1 - lev(e, g) / e.length);\n}\n\nfunction peopleScore(expected, got) {\n  if (!expected.length) return { fields: got.length ? 0 : 1, total: 1, correct: got.length ? 0 : 1, extra: got.length };\n  let correct = 0, total = 0;\n  const pool = [...got];\n  for (const p of expected) {\n    const i = pool.findIndex((q) => norm(q.name) === norm(p.name));\n    const q = i >= 0 ? pool.splice(i, 1)[0] : null;\n    for (const k of [\"name\", \"born\", \"died\"]) {\n      total++;\n      if (q && (q[k] ?? null) === (p[k] ?? null)) correct++;\n    }\n  }\n  return { correct, total, extra: pool.length };\n}\n\nasync function call(model, img) {\n  const t0 = performance.now();\n  let res, body;\n  try {\n    res = await fetch(`https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta/models/${model}:generateContent`, {\n      method: \"POST\",\n      headers: { \"content-type\": \"application/json\", \"x-goog-api-key\": KEY },\n      body: JSON.stringify({\n        contents: [{ role: \"user\", parts: [{ inline_data: { mime_type: \"image/jpeg\", data: img } }, { text: PROMPT }] }],\n        generationConfig: { temperature: 0 },\n      }),\n      signal: AbortSignal.timeout(240_000),\n    });\n    body = await res.json();\n  } catch (e) {\n    return { ms: Math.round(performance.now() - t0), error: `request failed: ${e.name}` };\n  }\n  const ms = Math.round(performance.now() - t0);\n  if (!res.ok) return { ms, error: `${res.status} ${body.error?.message ?? \"\"}`.slice(0, 200) };\n  const raw = (body.candidates?.[0]?.content?.parts ?? []).filter((p) => !p.thought).map((p) => p.text ?? \"\").join(\"\");\n  const usage = body.usageMetadata ?? {};\n  const json = raw.slice(raw.indexOf(\"{\"), raw.lastIndexOf(\"}\") + 1);\n  try {\n    return { ms, parsed: JSON.parse(json), raw, inTok: usage.promptTokenCount, outTok: (usage.candidatesTokenCount ?? 0) + (usage.thoughtsTokenCount ?? 0) };\n  } catch {\n    return { ms, error: \"unparseable JSON\", raw };\n  }\n}\n\nconst manifest = JSON.parse(await readFile(`${fixturesDir}/manifest.json`, \"utf8\"));\nconst results = [];\nfor (const f of manifest) {\n  const img = (await readFile(`${fixturesDir}/${f.file}`)).toString(\"base64\");\n  for (const model of MODELS) {\n    const r = await call(model, img);\n    const row = { file: f.file, era: f.era, model, ms: r.ms, inTok: r.inTok, outTok: r.outTok, error: r.error, got: r.parsed, raw: r.error ? r.raw : undefined };\n    if (r.parsed) {\n      row.text = textScore(f.text, r.parsed.text);\n      Object.assign(row, peopleScore(f.people, Array.isArray(r.parsed.people) ? r.parsed.people : []));\n    }\n    results.push(row);\n    await writeFile(outFile, JSON.stringify(results, null, 2));\n    console.error(`${f.file.padEnd(26)} ${model.padEnd(20)} ${r.error ? \"ERR \" + r.error : `text ${row.text.toFixed(2)} fields ${row.correct}/${row.total} extra ${row.extra} ${r.ms}ms`}`);\n  }\n}\nawait writeFile(outFile, JSON.stringify(results, null, 2));\n","numLines":97,"startLine":1,"totalLines":97}},"displayPath":"../../../../private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-anchildress1-git-personal-gravespeaker/a78fbb29-c412-483a-b679-0722adb27f13/scratchpad/bench/run.mjs"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"862aa155-3d47-417a-96b5-61146e6ffd25","timestamp":"2026-10-27T18:21:37.310Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nCalled the Read tool with the following input: {\"file_path\":\"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-anchildress1-git-personal-gravespeaker/a78fbb29-c412-483a-b679-0722adb27f13/scratchpad/bench/run.mjs\"}\n</system-reminder>"},{"content":"<system-reminder>\nResult of calling the Read tool:\n1\t// Throwaway OCR smoke run: same prompt and images for every model, scored against fixtures/manifest.json.\n2\timport { readFile, writeFile } from \"node:fs/promises\";\n3\t\n4\tconst [fixturesDir, outFile] = process.argv.slice(2);\n5\tconst KEY = process.env.GEMINI_API_KEY;\n6\tconst MODELS = [\"gemma-4-26b-a4b-it\", \"gemma-4-31b-it\", \"gemini-3.8-flash\"];\n7\t\n8\tconst PROMPT = `You are reading a photo of a gravestone for a historical research tool.\n9\t\n10\tTranscribe ONLY what is carved or cast on the stone. Do NOT add, guess, or complete anything you cannot see.\n11\t\n12\tReturn ONLY a JSON object, no prose, no code fences:\n13\t{\"text\": string|null, \"people\": [{\"name\": string, \"born\": string|null, \"died\": string|null}]}\n14\t\n15\t- text: every line of the inscription in order, joined with \"\\\\n\". Write \"[?]\" for a word you cannot read. null if nothing is legible.\n16\t- people: one entry per person commemorated. name exactly as carved. born/died as \"YYYY\" or \"YYYY-MM-DD\"; use \"?\" for an unreadable digit; null when the date is not on the stone. [] if no name is legible.\n17\t- A year that is not a birth or death (marriage length, erection date) is NOT a life date.`;\n18\t\n19\tconst norm = (s) => (s ?? \"\").toLowerCase().replace(/[^\\p{L}\\p{N}?]+/gu, \" \").trim();\n20\t\n21\tfunction lev(a, b) {\n22\t  const d = Array.from({ length: a.length + 1 }, (_, i) => [i]);\n23\t  for (let j = 1; j <= b.length; j++) d[0][j] = j;\n24\t  for (let i = 1; i <= a.length; i++)\n25\t    for (let j = 1; j <= b.length; j++)\n26\t      d[i][j] = Math.min(d[i - 1][j] + 1, d[i][j - 1] + 1, d[i - 1][j - 1] + (a[i - 1] === b[j - 1] ? 0 : 1));\n27\t  return d[a.length][b.length];\n28\t}\n29\t\n30\tfunction textScore(expected, got) {\n31\t  const e = norm(expected), g = norm(got);\n32\t  if (!e) return g ? 0 : 1;\n33\t  return Math.max(0, 1 - lev(e, g) / e.length);\n34\t}\n35\t\n36\tfunction peopleScore(expected, got) {\n37\t  if (!expected.length) return { fields: got.length ? 0 : 1, total: 1, correct: got.length ? 0 : 1, extra: got.length };\n38\t  let correct = 0, total = 0;\n39\t  const pool = [...got];\n40\t  for (const p of expected) {\n41\t    const i = pool.findIndex((q) => norm(q.name) === norm(p.name));\n42\t    const q = i >= 0 ? pool.splice(i, 1)[0] : null;\n43\t    for (const k of [\"name\", \"born\", \"died\"]) {\n44\t      total++;\n45\t      if (q && (q[k] ?? null) === (p[k] ?? null)) correct++;\n46\t    }\n47\t  }\n48\t  return { correct, total, extra: pool.length };\n49\t}\n50\t\n51\tasync function call(model, img) {\n52\t  const t0 = performance.now();\n53\t  let res, body;\n54\t  try {\n55\t    res = await fetch(`https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta/models/${model}:generateContent`, {\n56\t      method: \"POST\",\n57\t      headers: { \"content-type\": \"application/json\", \"x-goog-api-key\": KEY },\n58\t      body: JSON.stringify({\n59\t        contents: [{ role: \"user\", parts: [{ inline_data: { mime_type: \"image/jpeg\", data: img } }, { text: PROMPT }] }],\n60\t        generationConfig: { temperature: 0 },\n61\t      }),\n62\t      signal: AbortSignal.timeout(240_000),\n63\t    });\n64\t    body = await res.json();\n65\t  } catch (e) {\n66\t    return { ms: Math.round(performance.now() - t0), error: `request failed: ${e.name}` };\n67\t  }\n68\t  const ms = Math.round(performance.now() - t0);\n69\t  if (!res.ok) return { ms, error: `${res.status} ${body.error?.message ?? \"\"}`.slice(0, 200) };\n70\t  const raw = (body.candidates?.[0]?.content?.parts ?? []).filter((p) => !p.thought).map((p) => p.text ?? \"\").join(\"\");\n71\t  const usage = body.usageMetadata ?? {};\n72\t  const json = raw.slice(raw.indexOf(\"{\"), raw.lastIndexOf(\"}\") + 1);\n73\t  try {\n74\t    return { ms, parsed: JSON.parse(json), raw, inTok: usage.promptTokenCount, outTok: (usage.candidatesTokenCount ?? 0) + (usage.thoughtsTokenCount ?? 0) };\n75\t  } catch {\n76\t    return { ms, error: \"unparseable JSON\", raw };\n77\t  }\n78\t}\n79\t\n80\tconst manifest = JSON.parse(await readFile(`${fixturesDir}/manifest.json`, \"utf8\"));\n81\tconst results = [];\n82\tfor (const f of manifest) {\n83\t  const img = (await readFile(`${fixturesDir}/${f.file}`)).toString(\"base64\");\n84\t  for (const model of MODELS) {\n85\t    const r = await call(model, img);\n86\t    const row = { file: f.file, era: f.era, model, ms: r.ms, inTok: r.inTok, outTok: r.outTok, error: r.error, got: r.parsed, raw: r.error ? r.raw : undefined };\n87\t    if (r.parsed) {\n88\t      row.text = textScore(f.text, r.parsed.text);\n89\t      Object.assign(row, peopleScore(f.people, Array.isArray(r.parsed.people) ? r.parsed.people : []));\n90\t    }\n91\t    results.push(row);\n92\t    await writeFile(outFile, JSON.stringify(results, null, 2));\n93\t    console.error(`${f.file.padEnd(26)} ${model.padEnd(20)} ${r.error ? \"ERR \" + r.error : `text ${row.text.toFixed(2)} fields ${row.correct}/${row.total} extra ${row.extra} ${r.ms}ms`}`);\n94\t  }\n95\t}\n96\tawait writeFile(outFile, JSON.stringify(results, null, 2));\n97\t\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"e8fe1454-894d-486c-ada2-536b95330a4e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/anchildress1/git_personal/gravespeaker","sessionId":"a78fbb29-c412-483a-b679-0722adb27f13","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"test/benchmark-fixtures","slug":"shimmying-exploring-umbrella"}
