{"parentUuid":"b7f36ddc-27ae-444d-8619-d2ea9b56e163","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgTCxM7E6tiQH5WoJfeqL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_013s43gLEjyvqAXCc2Uf3E2W","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 -I - <<'EOF'\np=\"docs/PRD.md\"; s=open(p).read()\ndef rep(a,b):\n    global s\n    assert s.count(a)==1,a; s=s.replace(a,b)\nrep(\"\"\"- Measure actual recognition accuracy instead of assuming a vision model performs well.\n\"\"\",\"\"\"- Measure actual recognition accuracy instead of assuming a vision model performs well.\n- A deterministic layer in code parses names and strips and normalizes dates from the model output. The model reads the stone; code owns the format.\n\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"Model inference and historical search sit behind replaceable interfaces. Everything else stays concrete.\n\"\"\",\"\"\"Model inference and historical search sit behind replaceable interfaces. Everything else stays concrete.\n\nModel and search calls use Mastra's built-in retries and error handling. No hand-rolled retry loops.\n\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"- Paywalled or login-gated record sources\n\"\"\",\"\"\"- Paywalled or login-gated record sources\n- Multi-person (companion) stones: the app reads one person per stone\n- Optimizing for non-English inscriptions: nothing blocks them, but prompts and parsing target English\n\"\"\")\ns=s.rstrip(\"\\n\")+\"\"\"\n\n**Multi-person stones**\n\n- Tune the extraction prompts for companion stones, where two people share one surname line.\n- The MVP benchmark showed hosted Gemma reading every date on one but dropping the shared surname.\n\"\"\"\nopen(p,\"w\").write(s)\nEOF\npnpm exec prettier --write docs/PRD.md >/dev/null && git --no-pager diff","description":"Add non-goals, v2 entry, and code requirements to the PRD"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache