{"parentUuid":"2c5ec9b6-f0b8-4386-953f-47243791c4fa","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"35537cc9-ba97-458d-9db8-2b66ba5461e6","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013s43gLEjyvqAXCc2Uf3E2W","type":"tool_result","content":"diff --git a/docs/PRD.md b/docs/PRD.md\nindex b0854d6..32f8245 100644\n--- a/docs/PRD.md\n+++ b/docs/PRD.md\n@@ -48,6 +48,8 @@ If credible information can't be found, the app says so. It never fills historic\n \n Model inference and historical search sit behind replaceable interfaces. Everything else stays concrete.\n \n+Model and search calls use Mastra's built-in retries and error handling. No hand-rolled retry loops.\n+\n No self-hosted models unless benchmarks show a compelling advantage.\n \n ## 4. Key Engineering Challenges\n@@ -56,6 +58,7 @@ No self-hosted models unless benchmarks show a compelling advantage.\n \n - Weathered stone, damaged inscriptions, shadows, unusual typography and partial dates.\n - Measure actual recognition accuracy instead of assuming a vision model performs well.\n+- A deterministic layer in code parses names and strips and normalizes dates from the model output. The model reads the stone; code owns the format.\n \n **Historical identity resolution**\n \n@@ -125,6 +128,8 @@ The post focuses on the problem, engineering decisions, real discoveries, failur\n - Custom model hosting\n - Persistent user profiles and photo libraries\n - Paywalled or login-gated record sources\n+- Multi-person (companion) stones: the app reads one person per stone\n+- Optimizing for non-English inscriptions: nothing blocks them, but prompts and parsing target English\n \n ## 7. Privacy\n \n@@ -162,3 +167,8 @@ Not part of the October 31 build. Captured so the ideas aren't lost.\n - When the matched obituary has a photo, show it while the speaker is talking.\n - Display it from its original URL with a visible credit and link. Never download, cache or re-host it, and skip any image whose source restricts embedding.\n - This is the one deliberate exception to the \"link, don't republish\" rule in §4, so it needs a licensing check before it ships.\n+\n+**Multi-person stones**\n+\n+- Tune the extraction prompts for companion stones, where two people share one surname line.\n+- The MVP benchmark showed hosted Gemma reading every date on one but dropping the shared surname.\n[This command modified 1 file you've previously read: docs/PRD.md. Call Read before editing.]","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"9d9def56-dbb0-457e-86e1-d24428945ba2","timestamp":"2026-10-27T18:22:13.513Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"diff --git a/docs/PRD.md b/docs/PRD.md\nindex b0854d6..32f8245 100644\n--- a/docs/PRD.md\n+++ b/docs/PRD.md\n@@ -48,6 +48,8 @@ If credible information can't be found, the app says so. It never fills historic\n \n Model inference and historical search sit behind replaceable interfaces. Everything else stays concrete.\n \n+Model and search calls use Mastra's built-in retries and error handling. No hand-rolled retry loops.\n+\n No self-hosted models unless benchmarks show a compelling advantage.\n \n ## 4. Key Engineering Challenges\n@@ -56,6 +58,7 @@ No self-hosted models unless benchmarks show a compelling advantage.\n \n - Weathered stone, damaged inscriptions, shadows, unusual typography and partial dates.\n - Measure actual recognition accuracy instead of assuming a vision model performs well.\n+- A deterministic layer in code parses names and strips and normalizes dates from the model output. The model reads the stone; code owns the format.\n \n **Historical identity resolution**\n \n@@ -125,6 +128,8 @@ The post focuses on the problem, engineering decisions, real discoveries, failur\n - Custom model hosting\n - Persistent user profiles and photo libraries\n - Paywalled or login-gated record sources\n+- Multi-person (companion) stones: the app reads one person per stone\n+- Optimizing for non-English inscriptions: nothing blocks them, but prompts and parsing target English\n \n ## 7.